      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I mean, my avatars rank in as very poor, yet I lag nobody. The current system of rating is stupid. it turns on everything on the avatar all at once, then counts the amount of particles, meshes, texture slots, and vertices. \nI use this amazing thing called a \"toggle\", 95% of that stuff is turned OFF and not rendering for the end user, and thus not lagging their system, but vrchat acts like I can turn it all on at once. \nLiterally if i go \"turn on jacket\" it turns off the dang T-shirt that the jacket would cover, because as all games know, if you can't see it, it doesn't need to be rendered. \nVrchat's rating system acts like every single mesh on an avatar would -ever- be on at the same time, and let me tell you : if that could ever happen, you suck at logic. Why would i want my pants AND shorts on at the same time? Why would i want all 8 different kinds of shoes on at the same time? Why would i want 3 different kinds of weapons on at the same time? They all force each other to hide, so that people don't set their PC on fire when they look at me.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
